<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">King William's Town</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1835">1835</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Qonce</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King William's Town is a town on the Buffalo River in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-cape">Eastern Cape</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, founded in 1835 as a military headquarters during the frontier war against the Xhosa and named after King William IV. It was the seat of the short-lived Province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adelaide-of-saxe-meiningen">Queen Adelaide</a> and later the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-kaffraria">British Kaffraria</a>. It was officially renamed Qonce in 2021.</p></div>
